         <div type="bio">
            <p>Michigan bookseller and literature professor at Stephens College, Missouri. He edited the literary magazine<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Signatures: Work in Progress</name> (1936–38), and was himself a writer of fiction. In 1934, Thompson acquired the ‘Before Sunrise’ notebook, containing JJ’s translation of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Vor Sonnenaufgang</name> by <name type="person" key="haup62">Gerhart Hauptmann</name>. JJ, acting through <name type="person" key="leon93">Paul Léon</name>, refused Thompson permission to publish the translation, which in the 1970s was acquired by the Huntington Library and published as <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Joyce and Hauptmann: Before Sunrise: James Joyce's Translation</name>, ed. Jill Perkins (San Marino: Huntington Library, 1978) <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
